### 2.3 Motivation of the Thesis

In this thesis the measurement of the beauty contribution to non photonic electrons in p+p collisions at 500 GeV is investigated for the first time. This measurement is going to supplement the measurement of beauty contribution via e-h correlations which is the subject of another STAR thesis. Furthermore the production of \(D^{*}\) mesons in p+p collisions at 500 GeV is measured for the first time at a pT higher than 6.5 and up to 18 GeV applying a new method. The above measurements will constrain models trying to understand charm and beauty production at RHIC in p+p and A+A collisions and notably contribute to understand and interpret the suppression of heavy flavor in A+A at RHIC.

